---@field widthPx? number The maximum available width, in pixels.
---@field heightPx? number The maximum available height, in pixels.
---@field authorAttributions? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1AuthorAttributionList This photo's authors.
---@field flagContentUri? string A link where users can flag a problem with the photo.

---@alias gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PhotoList gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1Photo[]

---A photo media from Places API.
---@class gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PhotoMedia
---@field photoUri? string A short-lived uri that can be used to render the photo.
---@field name? string The resource name of a photo media in the format: `places/{place_id}/photos/{photo_reference}/media`.

---All the information representing a Place.
---@class gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1Place
---@field name? string This Place's resource name, in `places/{place_id}` format. Can be used to look up the Place.
---@field goodForChildren? boolean Place is good for children.
---@field id? string The unique identifier of a place.
---@field evChargeOptions? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1EVChargeOptions Information of ev charging options.
---@field allowsDogs? boolean Place allows dogs.
---@field pureServiceAreaBusiness? boolean Indicates whether the place is a pure service area business. Pure service area business is a business that visits or delivers to customers directly but does not serve customers at their business address. For example, businesses like cleaning services or plumbers. Those businesses may not have a physical address or location on Google Maps.
---@field shortFormattedAddress? string A short, human-readable address for this place.
---@field servesDessert? boolean Place serves dessert.
---@field timeZone? gcp.places_v1.GoogleTypeTimeZone IANA Time Zone Database time zone. For example "America/New_York".
---@field curbsidePickup? boolean Specifies if the business supports curbside pickup.
---@field addressDescriptor? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1AddressDescriptor The address descriptor of the place. Address descriptors include additional information that help describe a location using landmarks and areas. See address descriptor regional coverage in https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/geocoding/address-descriptors/coverage.
---@field servesVegetarianFood? boolean Specifies if the place serves vegetarian food.
---@field googleMapsLinks? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceGoogleMapsLinks Links to trigger different Google Maps actions.
---@field openingDate? gcp.places_v1.GoogleTypeDate The date this place will open in the future. This field is only populated if the business status is FUTURE_OPENING.
---@field servesBrunch? boolean Specifies if the place serves brunch.
---@field goodForGroups? boolean Place accommodates groups.
---@field servesBeer? boolean Specifies if the place serves beer.
---@field plusCode? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlacePlusCode Plus code of the place location lat/long.
---@field currentSecondaryOpeningHours? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceOpeningHoursList Contains an array of entries for the next seven days including information about secondary hours of a business. Secondary hours are different from a business's main hours. For example, a restaurant can specify drive through hours or delivery hours as its secondary hours. This field populates the type subfield, which draws from a predefined list of opening hours types (such as DRIVE_THROUGH, PICKUP, or TAKEOUT) based on the types of the place. This field includes the special_days subfield of all hours, set for dates that have exceptional hours.
---@field reviews? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1ReviewList List of reviews about this place, sorted by relevance. A maximum of 5 reviews can be returned.
---@field servesCocktails? boolean Place serves cocktails.
---@field fuelOptions? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1FuelOptions The most recent information about fuel options in a gas station. This information is updated regularly.
---@field formattedAddress? string A full, human-readable address for this place.
---@field primaryTypeDisplayName? gcp.places_v1.GoogleTypeLocalizedText The display name of the primary type, localized to the request language if applicable. For the complete list of possible values, see Table A and Table B at https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/place-types. The primary type may be missing if the place's primary type is not a supported type.
---@field primaryType? string The primary type of the given result. This type must be one of the Places API supported types. For example, "restaurant", "cafe", "airport", etc. A place can only have a single primary type. For the complete list of possible values, see Table A and Table B at https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/place-types. The primary type may be missing if the place's primary type is not a supported type. When a primary type is present, it is always one of the types in the `types` field.
---@field priceLevel? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlacePriceLevelEnum Price level of the place.
---@field servesDinner? boolean Specifies if the place serves dinner.
---@field dineIn? boolean Specifies if the business supports indoor or outdoor seating options.
---@field evChargeAmenitySummary? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceEvChargeAmenitySummary The summary of amenities near the EV charging station.
---@field rating? number A rating between 1.0 and 5.0, based on user reviews of this place.
---@field subDestinations? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceSubDestinationList A list of sub-destinations related to the place.
---@field restroom? boolean Place has restroom.
---@field menuForChildren? boolean Place has a children's menu.
---@field photos? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PhotoList Information (including references) about photos of this place. A maximum of 10 photos can be returned.
---@field types? gcp.places_v1.StringList A set of type tags for this result. For example, "political" and "locality". For the complete list of possible values, see Table A and Table B at https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/place-types
---@field iconBackgroundColor? string Background color for icon_mask in hex format, e.g. #909CE1.
---@field googleMapsTypeLabel? gcp.places_v1.GoogleTypeLocalizedText The type label of the place on Google Maps, localized to the request language if applicable, for example, "Restaurant", "Cafe", "Airport", etc. The type label may be different from the primary type display name and may not be a supported type in [Places API Place Types table](https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/place-types).
---@field servesCoffee? boolean Place serves coffee.
---@field location? gcp.places_v1.GoogleTypeLatLng The position of this place.
---@field websiteUri? string The authoritative website for this place, e.g. a business' homepage. Note that for places that are part of a chain (e.g. an IKEA store), this will usually be the website for the individual store, not the overall chain.
---@field userRatingCount? number The total number of reviews (with or without text) for this place.
---@field parkingOptions? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceParkingOptions Options of parking provided by the place.
---@field utcOffsetMinutes? number Number of minutes this place's timezone is currently offset from UTC. This is expressed in minutes to support timezones that are offset by fractions of an hour, e.g. X hours and 15 minutes.
---@field iconMaskBaseUri? string A truncated URL to an icon mask. User can access different icon type by appending type suffix to the end (eg, ".svg" or ".png").
---@field neighborhoodSummary? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceNeighborhoodSummary A summary of points of interest near the place.
---@field adrFormatAddress? string The place's address in adr microformat: http://microformats.org/wiki/adr.
---@field accessibilityOptions? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceAccessibilityOptions Information about the accessibility options a place offers.
---@field reviewSummary? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceReviewSummary AI-generated summary of the place using user reviews.
---@field priceRange? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PriceRange The price range associated with a Place.
---@field googleMapsUri? string A URL providing more information about this place.
---@field regularOpeningHours? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceOpeningHours The regular hours are the hours of operation for a place on a typical schedule. Note that if a place is always open (24 hours), the `close` field will not be set. Clients can rely on always open (24 hours) being represented as an [`open`](https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/reference/rest/v1/places#Period) period containing [`day`](https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/reference/rest/v1/places#Point) with value `0`, [`hour`](https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/reference/rest/v1/places#Point) with value `0`, and [`minute`](https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/reference/rest/v1/places#Point) with value `0`.
---@field postalAddress? gcp.places_v1.GoogleTypePostalAddress The address in postal address format.
---@field regularSecondaryOpeningHours? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceOpeningHoursList Contains an array of entries for information about regular secondary hours of a business. Secondary hours are different from a business's main hours. For example, a restaurant can specify drive through hours or delivery hours as its secondary hours. This field populates the type subfield, which draws from a predefined list of opening hours types (such as DRIVE_THROUGH, PICKUP, or TAKEOUT) based on the types of the place.
---@field internationalPhoneNumber? string A human-readable phone number for the place, in international format.
---@field containingPlaces? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceContainingPlaceList List of places in which the current place is located.
---@field reservable? boolean Specifies if the place supports reservations.
---@field businessStatus? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceBusinessStatusEnum The business status for the place.
---@field paymentOptions? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlacePaymentOptions Payment options the place accepts. If a payment option data is not available, the payment option field will be unset.
---@field servesBreakfast? boolean Specifies if the place serves breakfast.
---@field displayName? gcp.places_v1.GoogleTypeLocalizedText The localized name of the place, suitable as a short human-readable description. For example, "Google Sydney", "Starbucks", "Pyrmont", etc.
---@field addressComponents? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceAddressComponentList Repeated components for each locality level. Note the following facts about the address_components[] array: - The array of address components may contain more components than the formatted_address. - The array does not necessarily include all the political entities that contain an address, apart from those included in the formatted_address. To retrieve all the political entities that contain a specific address, you should use reverse geocoding, passing the latitude/longitude of the address as a parameter to the request. - The format of the response is not guaranteed to remain the same between requests. In particular, the number of address_components varies based on the address requested and can change over time for the same address. A component can change position in the array. The type of the component can change. A particular component may be missing in a later response.
---@field generativeSummary? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceGenerativeSummary AI-generated summary of the place.
---@field entrances? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceEntranceList Entrances for this destination.
---@field servesWine? boolean Specifies if the place serves wine.
---@field takeout? boolean Specifies if the business supports takeout.
---@field currentOpeningHours? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceOpeningHours The hours of operation for the next seven days (including today) incorporating any special opening hours. The time period starts at midnight on the date of the request and ends at 11:59 pm six days later. If the actual opening hours are outside of this range, the opening hours will be truncated. For example, if a place is open from 10pm yesterday to 6am today, the opening hours will be truncated to 12am today to 6am today. This field includes the special_days subfield of all hours, set for dates that have exceptional hours.
---@field transitStation? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1TransitStation The transit station information for the place.
---@field navigationPoints? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceNavigationPointList Navigation points for this destination.
---@field delivery? boolean Specifies if the business supports delivery.
---@field viewport? gcp.places_v1.GoogleGeoTypeViewport A viewport suitable for displaying the place on an average-sized map. This viewport should not be used as the physical boundary or the service area of the business.
---@field movedPlaceId? string If this Place is permanently closed and has moved to a new Place, this field contains the new Place's place ID. If this Place moved multiple times, this field will represent the first moved Place. This field will not be populated if this Place has not moved.
---@field goodForWatchingSports? boolean Place is suitable for watching sports.
---@field movedPlace? string If this Place is permanently closed and has moved to a new Place, this field contains the new Place's resource name, in `places/{place_id}` format. If this Place moved multiple times, this field will represent the first moved place. This field will not be populated if this Place has not moved.
---@field nationalPhoneNumber? string A human-readable phone number for the place, in national format.
---@field attributions? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceAttributionList A set of data provider that must be shown with this result.
---@field outdoorSeating? boolean Place provides outdoor seating.
---@field editorialSummary? gcp.places_v1.GoogleTypeLocalizedText Contains a summary of the place. A summary is comprised of a textual overview, and also includes the language code for these if applicable. Summary text must be presented as-is and can not be modified or altered.
---@field liveMusic? boolean Place provides live music.
---@field consumerAlert? gcp.places_v1.GoogleMapsPlacesV1PlaceConsumerAlert The consumer alert message for the place when we detect suspicious review activity on a business or a business violates our policies.
---@field servesLunch? boolean Specifies if the place serves lunch.

